  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fiji Institutional Partnerships Program (IPP) supports Government of Fiji (GoF) priorities. Australian partners were flexible and responsive to GoF priorities, enabling GoF to strengthen public financial management, policy and processes across civil service, elections, and media sector. This was facilitated through the provision of technical assistance, training, exchanges, and flexible funding modalities to support Government ministries and statutory agencies. 
&#x200d;
Through Australia&#x2019;s support, Fiji Bureau of Statistics (FBOS) has developed a publicly available dashboard comprising population and housing data from the latest census, which can be disaggregated into seven dashboards, including Sex, Age Group; Major Ethnic Groups; Martial Status; Major Religious Groups; Employment Status; Disability and Youth (15-35 years old). The housing dashboard allows the user to view the number of Households broken down by Living Quarters; Types of Floor, Roof and Walls; and Access to Sanitation. The aim of this work is to improve data use for planning and decision-making using simple visualization tools. The dashboard has also eliminated the burden on the FBOS team to gather data manually and prepare bespoke reports based on requests. This has also strengthened transparency and accountability by making data more accessible.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Fiji-Australia Institutional Partnership Program, Australia has supported gender-responsive budgeting (GRB) reform in Fiji, in partnership with the Asian Development Bank. In 2021, the Fiji Ministry of Economy included GRB in the Budget Circular, requiring two Ministries to consider gender as part of their budget submissions. Building on lessons from the 2021 pilot, eight ministries and the Fiji Police Force implemented and monitored GRB allocations for 14 programs in 2022, institutionalizing the new gender-responsive budgeting methodology and enabling a more equitable allocation of resources and outcomes for women, including those in vulnerable situations such as experiencing poverty.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
